    "terminal_reason": "completed",
    "result_text": "I've implemented `find_candidates` in `app/catalog.py` and added a test for it; both tests in the suite pass.\n\nIt makes one listing request, `api.list_models(search=name_fragment, pipeline_tag=task, sort=\"downloads\", limit=limit)`, and returns the model ids in the order the Hub gives them. I checked the installed huggingface_hub 2.0.0: all four arguments are sent to the Hub as query parameters, and the client stops after `limit` results, so it never fetches everything. Downloads are sorted most-downloaded first, and version 2.0.0 no longer has a `direction` argument, so I didn't pass one.\n\n- **Extra argument:** I added an optional `api: HfApi | None = None` argument, the same as `org_models` and `model_stats` have, so the new test can pass in a fake client. Existing calls with three arguments work unchanged.\n- **What the test covers:** `tests/test_catalog.py` checks that exactly those arguments reach `list_models`. It uses the existing fake client, so nothing was checked against the real Hub.\n- **Private models:** If you're logged in to Hugging Face on that machine, the Hub may also return private models you have access to. If the shortlist must be strictly public, pass `token=False` in the call."
  },
